### Delivered: `pipeline_refactored.py`

| Requirement | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| **Config** | `DB_PATH`, `LOG_FILE`, `DB_HOST`, `DB_PORT`, `DB_USER`, `DB_PASS` hardcoded at module level | All via `os.environ.get()` with matching defaults — `LOG_FILE_PATH`, `DB_PATH`, `REPORT_PATH` |
| **SQL injection** | `"INSERT ... VALUES ('%s', '%s', %d)" % (now, msg, count)` — string formatting of user data | `"INSERT ... VALUES (?, ?, ?)"` — parameterized via `conn.execute()` tuple args |
| **Structure** | One monolithic `proc_data()` function | 8 functions in ETL phases: `read_log_lines` → `parse_log_line` / `aggregate_logs` → `init_db` / `load_error_summary` / `load_api_metrics` / `generate_report_html` / `write_html`, plus a `main()` orchestrator |
| **Log parsing** | `line.split(" ")` with fragile index magic (`s[2]`, `s[3]`) | Three named-capture regex patterns (`LINE_RE`, `USER_RE`, `API_RE`) |
| **Type hints** | None | Full annotations on all functions + `LogEntry`, `LogSummary`, `Config` frozen dataclasses with `slots=True` |
| **Docstrings** | None | All public functions documented (PEP 257) |
| **File I/O** | Bare `f = open(...)` / `f.close()` | `with open(...) as f:` context managers; `Path().write_text()` for HTML output |

